WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.630
Draw a hump: y equals f of x.

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.150
Put a two outside: y equals two f of x.

3
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.710
The hump grows twice as tall.

4
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.940
Put the two inside the
bracket: y equals f of two x.

5
00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.690
The hump shrinks to half as wide.

6
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.890
Same number, same function.

7
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:23.090
So why does one two stretch it
up, and the other pull it in?

8
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:27.140
In this mission, you'll sketch cubics
and quartics from their factors,

9
00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:29.820
and reciprocal graphs
with their asymptotes.

10
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:32.670
And you'll transform graphs: translations,

11
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.810
reflections and stretches.

12
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:39.750
Your mission: explain why the same two
makes one graph narrower and the other

13
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:40.520
taller.
